ASIC synthesis is carried out using synthesis tools that employ standard cell libraries, constraints, and primarily RTL code to generate a gate-level netlist. Synopsys Design Compiler stands as a prominent ASIC synthesis tool widely embraced in the industry. Moreover, open-source toolchains such as OpenROAD are integral components of the broader initiative to advance open-source IC design~\cite{openroad}. OpenROAD specifically concentrates on developing a fully autonomous toolchain for digital SoC synthesis and layout generation, contributing to the open-source ecosystem.

